course: dictionary
lesson: 6397
title: A mural is a picture on a wall
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mural is a large picture painted straight onto a wall or a ceiling. The word tells you two things: it is big, and it is part of the building, not a small picture hung on a nail. «Classes may design a mural for the playground» tells you the picture is made for a place, and that place is a wall.
explain: Look at the words around mural to check. «A school mural» tells you it belongs to a school. «A street mural» tells you people walking past can see it outside. Each phrase gives you a clue about where the picture is and who it is for.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the word. «Sam suggested a long mural on the underpass wall» still works if you put "a long picture painted on the underpass wall" in its place. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A mural is a large picture painted directly onto a wall or ceiling.
fact: Common phrases are «paint a mural», «a school mural», «a street mural» and «a wall mural».
fact: Murals can show local history, heroes or nature.
fact: «A mural is a big wall painting done with permission, often paid for by councils, building owners or festivals.»
fact: Cave paintings and church wall paintings are early murals.
exercise: Classes may design «a mural for the playground». What is a mural? | A game played at break | A small sketch on paper | A kind of school bell | *A large picture painted onto a wall or ceiling
exercise: «A huge mural on a block of flats, paid for by the council, is legal and often loved.» Why is this mural legal? | *It was agreed and paid for by the council | It was sprayed on a bus shelter without asking | It was painted in secret at night | It was drawn on a piece of paper
exercise: Which of these is a mural? | A photo hung in a frame | A name sprayed on a bus shelter | *A long picture painted on a school wall with permission | A sketch on paper for later
test: «Since 2014, many murals in Ukrainian cities show hope, heroes and national symbols.» What do these murals show? | Shopping lists for the week | *Hope, heroes and national symbols | Only sports cars | Lost pets and missing bikes
test: Why are good murals planned on paper first? | To hide the wall from the owner | To avoid asking anyone for permission | To make the picture smaller than the wall | *To plan a sketch and a grid before painting
exam: What does mural mean in «Sam suggested a long mural on the underpass wall»? | A long walk | A game of cards | A tunnel under a road | *A large painting on a wall
